# ETHAN WebUI $\rightarrow$ Open-WebUI Migration Plan

This document tracks the transformation of the ETHAN WebUI into a high-fidelity interface based on Open-WebUI.

## Architectural Principle
**Open-WebUI UX + ETHAN Capabilities = ETHAN WebUI**
The WebUI is a stateless presentation layer. All business logic, state, and persistence reside in ETHAN Core/API.

---

## Implementation Roadmap

### P0: Core Shell & Navigation (Critical Path)
- [x] **Root Layout**: Narrow sidebar with logo and primary navigation.
- [x] **App Layout**: Main shell with wide sidebar and content slot.
- [x] **Wide Sidebar**:
    - [x] New Chat & Search buttons.
    - [x] Pinned Menu items (Notes -> Missions, Workspace -> Dashboard, etc.).
    - [x] Chat List with time-range grouping.
    - [x] Pinned Chats.
    - [x] User Profile Menu.
    - [x] Sidebar Resizing.
- [x] **Navigation**: Routing for `/`, `/c/:id`, `/settings`, etc.
- [x] **Model Selector**: High-fidelity model picker with search and categories.
- [x] **Settings**: User and Admin settings panels.

### P1: Workspace & Knowledge (Productivity)
- [ ] **Workspace**: Central hub for managing models, knowledge, and tools.
- [ ] **Knowledge**: Document management, upload, and association.
- [ ] **Skills/Tools/MCP**: Interface for activating and configuring capabilities.
- [ ] **Files**: File explorer and upload management.
- [ ] **Providers**: Backend connection management.

### P2: Advanced UX & Polish (Enhancements)
- [ ] **Memories**: Interface for managing long-term memory.
- [ ] **Tags & Collections**: Organizing chats and knowledge.
- [ ] **Prompts**: Prompt library and templates.
- [ ] **Advanced Functions**: Pipeline and agent configuration.
- [ ] **UX Polish**: Transitions, animations, and theme refinements.

